.TH "CITADEL" "1" "Sep 2026" "AceTeam" "Citadel CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
citadel-update-install - Download and install the latest version


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcitadel update install [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Downloads the latest version from GitHub, verifies the checksum,
backs up the current version, and installs the new binary.

.PP
If the new version fails to start, it will automatically roll back
to the previous version.

.PP
If citadel is running as a managed service (systemd/launchd/Windows
service), swapping the binary on disk does NOT restart the already-running
process -- it keeps executing the old code until something restarts it
(citadel#454). This command detects that and warns loudly by default; pass
--restart to have it restart the managed service for you.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for install

.PP
\fB--restart\fP[=false]
	Restart the managed citadel service (if any) after installing, so the new binary actually runs. Before restarting, waits up to 30s for the running worker's in-flight jobs to finish (best-effort, via GET /worker; citadel#887) -- restarts anyway once that elapses. If /worker is unreachable (an older worker predating the route, or no status listener at all) the wait is skipped entirely and this restarts immediately, same as before #887. Unlike the automatic AGENT_UPDATE/auto-updater paths, this is not a hard drain: it does not stop new jobs from being picked up while waiting.


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug output

.PP
\fB--no-auto-update\fP[=false]
	Disable automatic update checks and installs for this run (or set CITADEL_NO_AUTO_UPDATE=1)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	Disable colorized output

.PP
\fB--node-dir\fP=""
	Override the node config directory (citadel.yaml + services/), bypassing $HOME/ConfigDir resolution. Also settable via CITADEL_NODE_DIR. Scope: manifest/services resolution only -- does NOT redirect network state, the module lockfile, or nodevault.

.PP
\fB--runtime\fP=""
	Container runtime for module containers: docker or podman (default: auto-detect)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcitadel-update(1)\fP
